# WTABT.KEY - the key script of the tab strip's test, TEST/WTABT.C; every
# mode of Windows writes TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/WTABT.SNP, which TEST/tabchk.py
# checks.  The dialog: the strip, its tabs "Overview|Technical|
# Ac&quisition|Notes", the Edit after it in the tab order with the focus,
# and the Static "SEEN n CUR c": n the notifications, c the current tab
# the last one or WTM_SETCUR's answer reported.
S START
# CTRL-TAB from the Edit: the next tab, and from the last the first.
K CTRL-TAB
S CTAB
K CTRL-TAB CTRL-TAB
S CTAB3
K CTRL-TAB
S CTABWRAP
# CTRL-SHIFT-TAB: from the first the last, then the one before.
K CTRL-SHIFT-TAB
S CSTABWRP
K CTRL-SHIFT-TAB
S CSTAB
# LEFT in the Edit is the Edit's.
K LEFT
S EDITLEFT
# SHIFT-TAB gives the strip the focus; RIGHT and LEFT move one, none past
# the last or the first.
K SHIFT-TAB
S FOCUS
K RIGHT
S RIGHT
K RIGHT
S RIGHTEND
K LEFT LEFT LEFT
S LEFT0
K LEFT
S LEFTEND
# CTRL-TAB with the focus on the strip; TAB gives the Edit the focus.
K CTRL-TAB
S CTABFOC
K TAB
S TAB
# ALT and a mnemonic: Q is Acquisition's, T Technical's; T again is the
# current tab's, A (Acquisition's first letter, not its mnemonic) and Z
# are no tab's.
K ALT-Q
S ALTQ
K ALT-T
S ALTT
K ALT-T
S ALTTCUR
K ALT-A
S ALTA
K ALT-Z
S ALTZ
# F2 clicks tab 2; SHIFT-F2 the current tab, CTRL-F2 right of the last
# tab, each from the Edit: the focus either way, a notification only for
# a new tab.
K F2
S CLICK2
K TAB
S TAB2
K SHIFT-F2
S CLICKCUR
K TAB
S TAB3
K CTRL-F2
S CLICKOUT
# F3 makes tab 3 current; SHIFT-F3 asks for tab 4, just past the last,
# which is none, and its rectangle, which it has not; F4 leaves two
# tabs, the current one now the last.  None notifies.
K F3
S SETCUR
K SHIFT-F3
S SETNONE
K F4
S TEXT
# The new tabs: CTRL-TAB wraps from the last, T is Two's.
K CTRL-TAB
S TEXTCTAB
K ALT-T
S TEXTALTT
# F5 sets thirteen tabs in more than WT_MAXTEXT bytes: only the first
# WT_MAXTABS count, so CTRL-SHIFT-TAB wraps from the first to the
# eighth, and CTRL-TAB from it to the first.
K F5
S MANY
K CTRL-SHIFT-TAB
S MANY0
K CTRL-SHIFT-TAB
S MANYWRAP
K CTRL-TAB
S MANYCTAB
# CTRL-PGUP wraps from the first to the eighth, CTRL-PGDN from it to the
# first, then on to the second.
K CPGUP
S PGUPWRAP
K CPGDN
S PGDNWRAP
K CPGDN
S PGDN
K ESC
